# GDPR / data residency (always — security compliance)

Resume: `@gdpr$` / `$residency$`. Same standing as `feature-data-classification-security.mdc`: **do not wait for the owner to ask.**

Owner (14 Nov 2026): European user data must move to **Firebase/Firestore hosting in Europe** to respect GDPR. Middle East data location is **undecided**. This is a **security compliance requirement**.

## Current vs required

| Now | Required |
|---|---|
| Project `shoutoutdemo-5b402`, Functions + Firestore **`us-central1`** | EU / EEA / UK patron PII system of record in Europe (`eur3` or `europe-west1` / `europe-west3`) |
| US-only is the live default | US may stay US; **EU PII must not remain US-only as the end state** |
